        "created_at": "2026-11-16T04:32:14.090Z",
        "note": {
          "id": 4241057092,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@jay_mccure The workplan for this issue is ready for review in the Workplan widget.\n\nIt covers an agent-facing, one-line stale bundled-skill notice after an upgrade. Detection stays on the existing content-hash check. The change is in `internal/commands/update/post_upgrade.go` and `skill_updates.go`, plus tests and docs.\n\nPlease check these before handing it to an implementer:\n- **Open MRs:** I could not read the diffs of https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4424 and https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4422 through the API. Step 1 is to compare them with the plan and build on !4424 instead of opening a third implementation.\n- **Opt-out:** the plan lets the agent notice follow `notify_skill_updates` and ignore `show_whats_new`. Confirm that is what you want.\n- **Duo Developer:** I treated whether Duo Developer environments carry stale copies as informational. I could not verify it from the repo.\n\nI posted no questions, so none are open. The work is one sequential track, so I did not split it into child items.",
          "author": {
